{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A persistent CI inspection error prevents later PRs in the repository from being observed."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"state","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A failure that recovers during a main-red pause is permanently omitted from the persisted ledger."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A casing difference in a valid repository slug prevents classification and can block subsequent PR observations."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"If a later partial attempt omits the tracked job, its completed rerun remains unresolved; the reproduction uses a simulated GitHub response."},{"id":"C5","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A rerun outside the first 100 observed contexts can finish without its outcome ever being recorded."},{"id":"C6","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A standard Node test timeout is classified as needing a fix rather than receiving the requested rerun."},{"id":"C7","consequence":"bypass","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A standard Playwright security-test failure heading can bypass the exclusion and allow an automatic rerun."},{"id":"C8","consequence":"outage","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Repeated REST inspections across paused PRs can exhaust GitHub API quota and disrupt factory operations."},{"id":"C9","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A stale persisted push marker after a crash can hide remote PR closure and other observations until it is cleared."},{"id":"C10","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A rate-limited rerun request can remain pending indefinitely without a retry or a needs-fix result."},{"id":"C11","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Lagging check data can cause a passed rerun to be reported as needing a fix."},{"id":"C12","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Multiple failing checks produce duplicate main-red feed alerts for one repository."},{"id":"C13","consequence":"bypass","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A main-branch legacy status can be missed when the PR uses a check run, bypassing the main-red pause."},{"id":"C14","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A CI failure first observed as a tracked PR closes is emitted but never classified or recorded."},{"id":"C15","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A rerun ending neutral or skipped remains pending indefinitely without a terminal ledger outcome."},{"id":"C16","consequence":"diag","trigger":"normal","reason":"Long setup output can displace failure context from the feed excerpt, although the signature still contains the selected failure line."},{"id":"C17","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"normal","reason":"Common setup text can be selected as the failure signature, conflating unrelated failures and obscuring their reports."},{"id":"C18","consequence":"diag","trigger":"normal","reason":"The different quoting convention is a style concern, with no demonstrated runtime defect."},{"id":"C20","consequence":"diag","trigger":"normal","reason":"The extra ordered migration successfully creates the intended schema and is only a maintainability preference."},{"id":"C21","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A nonsecurity check name containing 'sast', such as disaster recovery, suppresses its timeout rerun and ledger entry."},{"id":"C22","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"normal","reason":"Fail-fast matrix cancellations can be rerun and incorrectly recorded as flakes."},{"id":"C6b","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An indented untimestamped Playwright timeout is classified as needing a fix instead of being rerun."},{"id":"C7b","consequence":"bypass","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A standard Go security-test failure heading can bypass the exclusion and allow an automatic rerun."}]}